                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003063"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The formation of the prechordal plate. The prechordal plate is a thickening of the endoderm at the cranial end of the primitive streak formed by the involution of Spemann&apos;s organizer cells. The prechordal plate and the notochord induce the formation of the neural plate from the overlying ectodermal cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>biological_process</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>GO:0021501</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>prechordal plate formation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0021501"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The formation of the prechordal plate. The prechordal plate is a thickening of the endoderm at the cranial end of the primitive streak formed by the involution of Spemann&apos;s organizer cells. The prechordal plate and the notochord induce the formation of the neural plate from the overlying ectodermal cells.</owl:annotatedTarget>
