        <owl:annotatedTarget>The process whose specific outcome is the progression of a tube over time, from its initial formation to a mature structure. Epithelial and endothelial tubes transport gases, liquids and cells from one site to another and form the basic structure of many organs and tissues including lung and trachea, kidney, the mammary gland, the vascular system and the gastrointestinal and urinary-genital tracts.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:12526790</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


