            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any process that results in a change in state or activity of a cell or an organism (in terms of movement, secretion, enzyme production, gene expression, etc.) as a result of a norepinephrine stimulus. Norepinephrine is a catecholamine that has the formula C8H11NO3; it acts as a hormone, and as a neurotransmitter in most of the sympathetic nervous system.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>mah</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2010-09-13T03:31:53Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>response to noradrenaline stimulus</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>response to norepinephrine stimulus</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>biological_process</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>GO:0071873</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Note that epinephrine and norepinephrine are ligands for the same receptors, and there are multiple adrenergic receptors.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>response to norepinephrine</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
