        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Setose as a label is used extensively to describe insect phenotypes that have hairy-like appearances (i.e., they are covered in setae, not the hairs of mammals). A bristle is a type of seta.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>setose</rdfs:label>
