    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102001 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102001">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A characteristic used to describe another characteristic.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7356-1779</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2026-05-05T00:00:00Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>quality</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>meta characteristic</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>PATO:0102001</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Instances of modifier characteristic should NOT be linked to their bearers via &apos;characteristic of&apos; (RO:0000052) or its inverse &apos;has characteristic&apos; (RO:0000053). Use &apos;has modifier&apos; (RO:0002573) to connect a modifier characteristic to the characteristic it modifies. This keeps &apos;characteristic of&apos; / &apos;has characteristic&apos; restricted to entity-or-process-to-characteristic relations.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>modifier characteristic</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102001"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A characteristic used to describe another characteristic.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/602</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102001"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>meta characteristic</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OBO:earlier-draft</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102002 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102002">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A modifier characteristic determined by comparison to a reference.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7356-1779</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2026-05-05T00:00:00Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>quality</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>comparison modifier</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>state modifier</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>PATO:0102002</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>A comparative modifier characteristic is relational - its identity (e.g. increased vs decreased, abnormal vs normal) is fixed by comparison to a reference. The broader &apos;modifier characteristic&apos; also covers non-comparative modifiers (intensity, magnitude, secondary).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>comparative modifier characteristic</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102002"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A modifier characteristic determined by comparison to a reference.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/602</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102002"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>comparison modifier</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OBO:earlier-draft</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102002"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>state modifier</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OBO:earlier-draft</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102003 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102003">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102002"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A comparative modifier characteristic indicating that the bearer characteristic has a value greater than a reference.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002604 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102004"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7356-1779</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2026-05-05T00:00:00Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>quality</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>PATO:0102003</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Usage (agreed uPheno call 2026-06-12): &apos;increased&apos; is only to be used to define pre-coordinated value terms via &apos;has modifier&apos; (RO:0002573), e.g. &apos;increased weight&apos; EquivalentTo &apos;weight and has_modifier some increased&apos;. Do NOT use &apos;increased&apos; directly in phenotype patterns, and do NOT use it as an is_a parent of a domain characteristic. If a pre-coordinated value term exists for the bearer and direction, use that term; if none exists, request that it be added. Distinct from the now-obsolete PATO:0002300 (increased quality), which was a grouping class for pre-coordinated physical/process qualities.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>increased</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102003"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A comparative modifier characteristic indicating that the bearer characteristic has a value greater than a reference.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/602</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102004 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102004">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102002"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A comparative modifier characteristic indicating that the bearer characteristic has a value less than a reference.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002604 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102003"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7356-1779</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2026-05-05T00:00:00Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>quality</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>PATO:0102004</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Usage (agreed uPheno call 2026-06-12): &apos;decreased&apos; is only to be used to define pre-coordinated value terms via &apos;has modifier&apos; (RO:0002573), e.g. &apos;decreased weight&apos; EquivalentTo &apos;weight and has_modifier some decreased&apos;. Do NOT use &apos;decreased&apos; directly in phenotype patterns, and do NOT use it as an is_a parent of a domain characteristic. If a pre-coordinated value term exists for the bearer and direction, use that term; if none exists, request that it be added. Distinct from the now-obsolete PATO:0002301 (decreased quality), which was a grouping class for pre-coordinated physical/process qualities.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>decreased</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0102004"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A comparative modifier characteristic indicating that the bearer characteristic has a value less than a reference.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/602</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0103000 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0103000">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>OBSOLETE. A quality of an entity that can be represented numerically, including anything that can be counted, measured, or given a numerical value.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8314-2140</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>quality</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>PATO:0103000</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Obsoleted in https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/602. The qualitative/quantitative dichotomy has no role in the new upper model. The single direct child (amount, PATO:0000070) has been moved under physical object characteristic.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>obsolete quantitative</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0103000"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>OBSOLETE. A quality of an entity that can be represented numerically, including anything that can be counted, measured, or given a numerical value.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://libguides.macalester.edu/c.php?g=527786&amp;p=3608639</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.nnlm.gov/guides/data-glossary/quantitative-data</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0103001 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0103001">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A quantitative quality that represents the sum of all &apos;mass&apos; qualities of the component parts that constitute a whole entity. The total mass quality inheres in the whole entity and reflects the aggregate measure of mass across all its components, such that changes in the mass of individual components may not necessarily correspond to equivalent changes in the total mass of the whole.

Example of usage: &quot;total body mass&quot; represents the sum of the masses of all tissues and organs in the body, while &quot;liver mass&quot; represents only the mass of the liver. An increase in liver mass does not necessarily mean an increase in total body mass, as the mass of other organs or tissues may decrease simultaneously.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2025-04-10T16:14:12Z</dc:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>quality</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>PATO:0103001</oboInOwl:id>
        <terms3:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8314-2140"/>
        <rdfs:label>total mass</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0103002 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0103002">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0103001"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0015007"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000461"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001563"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0103001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A total mass which is higher than normal or average.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2025-04-10T16:25:35Z</dc:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>quality</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>PATO:0103002</oboInOwl:id>
        <terms3:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8314-2140"/>
        <rdfs:label>increased total mass</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0103003 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0103003">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0103001"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0015008"/>
